        {
          "id": 2472190525,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "(Sorry it took me awhile to get back to this, but I was curious)\n\nI tried your tshark command above, but then I tried:\ntshark -q -z expert,warning,tcp -z expert,error,dhcp -r some_file.pcapng\n\n(i.e. swapping the two -z parameters because error level > warning level)\n\nand you only get error level expert info _without your patch_.  I think I was more surprised that 2 taps were actually registered, I was expecting a \"single expert tap\" (whose level was modified twice with last one winning) and that's originally why I thought your patch didn't matter. And I guess I agree that *shark _should_ create 2 taps in this situation.",
          "author": {
